[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127512,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Superficial acral fibromyxoma is a benign fibroblastic neoplasm typically restricted to acral sites with a marked predilection for the periungual region of the digits and potential for local recurrence.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127513,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8811/0 Superficial acral fibromyxoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127514,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EE6Y &amp; XH8173 Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue &amp; Acral fibromyxoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127515,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> digital fibromyxoma; acral fibromyxoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> cellular digital fibroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127516,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127517,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The great majority arise in the periungual/subungual region of the fingers and toes, with occasional cases involving the hands, feet, ankles, wrists, lower legs, and thighs {11486169; 19236516; 18537858; 18764846; 22367301; 27825811}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127518,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Acral fibromyxomas are slowly growing and often painful, and they range in size from 10&nbsp;to 50&nbsp;mm (mean: ~20&nbsp;mm) {11486169; 18537858; 22367301}. Associated nail deformities and lytic lesions of underlying bone may be seen {22367301; 18327578; 29423724}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127519,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The age range is wide, but most cases occur in middle-aged adults, with a male predilection {11486169; 22367301}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127520,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127521,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>RB1</em> deletions have been reported {27825811}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127522,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Acral fibromyxomas are dome-shaped, polypoid, or verrucous, often with a lobulated appearance. They have a firm to soft consistency and poorly defined borders.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127523,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Acral fibromyxomas are lobulated dermal and subcutaneous lesions, sometimes with an epidermal collarette. Most have infiltrative borders and the underlying bone may be involved. Most are relatively hypocellular, composed of bland spindled to stellate cells in a loose growth pattern that can be vaguely fascicular to storiform. Tumour cells are embedded in a variably collagenous to myxoid stroma, and a thin-walled vasculature may be present in myxoid areas. Multinucleated cells may be present. Mitotic figures are rare {11486169; 18537858; 18764846; 22367301; 28045748}. A subset may have increased cellularity {19236516}. Cartilaginous and osseous metaplasia is rare {29360681}.</p>\r\n<h6>Immunohistochemistry</h6>\r\n<p>The tumour cells are positive for CD34, CD99, and nestin and may express EMA and SMA in a minority; they are negative for MUC4 and BCL2 {11486169; 28045748; 22367301}. Loss of RB1 expression is seen in most tumours {27825811}.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>The stromal component of onychomatricoma is identical to that of acral fibromyxoma, but acral fibromyxoma lacks an epithelial component. Myxoid neurofibroma is less cellular and the tumour cells are positive for S100. Myxoid dermatofibrosarcoma protuberans is very rare on the digits and lacks the collagen component, and the tumour cells display a storiform pattern.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127524,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127525,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours show deletion of <em>RB1</em> {27825811}, but this is not required for diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127526,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> acral location, usually periungual; a lobulated dermal and subcutaneous tumour with bland spindled to stellate cells; variably myxoid to collagenous stroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> CD34 positivity; frequent loss of RB1 expression by immunohistochemistry.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127527,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127528,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 236,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These lesions are benign, but recurrence occurs in as many as 22% of cases {27825811; 22367301}. Metastases have not been reported {11486169; 22367301}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:53:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]